"P79690300" "The Magic Man"
// requiresfailedtext :
"P2251523409" "You must be a member of the Midnighter Club to access this mission."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - BlackDragonHideoutClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P409644104" "Black Dragon"
// DetailString :
"P3487874359" "The Tsoo tell you that they don't know anything about the Magic Man, but they have heard their boss, <color red>Black Dragon</color>, mention him before. They tell you about a warehouse where Black Dragon is at right now."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - BlackDragonInterrogatedClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P97632770" "The Magic Man is Family"
// DetailString :
"P1344650531" "Black Dragon gladly informs you that the Magic Man works for <color red>Jimmy the Preacher</color>, a Family Consigliere who has been giving the Tsoo a lot of trouble in Independence Port lately."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mission1Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P237148219" "The Magic Man"
// DetailString :
"P1340383786" "Amanda Gates ratted out her accomplice, the Magic Man, so you went over to Independence Port to question the Tsoo, figuring the Magic Man must be one of their leaders. As it turned out, the Tsoo were clueless, so you went after one of their leaders, a man by the name of Black Dragon. You infiltrated Black Dragon's illegal superadine shipping operation and forced him to tell you everything he knew about the Magic Man. According to him, the Magic Man was in the Family and worked for a man known as Jimmy the Preacher."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - MickeyMaloneyClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3093304411" "Mickey "The Magic Man" Maloney"
// DetailString :
"P2077445571" "Jimmy the Preacher tells you that the Magic Man and some Family goons are heading to a cargo ship in Independence Port with the intention of blowing it up.<br><br>Jimmy also tells you that the Magic Man used to be just another punk in a cheap suit who did dirty jobs for the Family, back when he was just known as Mickey Maloney. But when Maloney started taking down the Tsoo with regularity, though, he earned the nickname of 'the Magic Man'."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mission2Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P365877922" "Amanda Gates ratted out her accomplice, the Magic Man, so you went over to Independence Port to question the Tsoo, figuring the Magic Man must be one of their leaders. As it turned out, the Tsoo were clueless, so you went after one of their leaders, a man by the name of Black Dragon. You infiltrated Black Dragon's illegal superadine shipping operation and forced him to tell you everything he knew about the Magic Man. According to him, the Magic Man was in the Family and worked for a man known as Jimmy the Preacher.<br><br>You went over to Jimmy the Preacher's office to ask him some questions. After busting through Jimmy's buttonmen you made him talk. He told you that the Magic Man used to just be a buttonman named Mickey Maloney until he started taking down the Tsoo like they were nothing. Jimmy promoted him and that's how he earned the nickname of the Magic Man."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - BigTonysClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1126122521" "Big Tony's Clue"
// DetailString :
"P2553722415" "After rousing Big Tony from his forcefully induced nap you ask him a few hard questions. It doesn't take him long to spill his guts about the Warriors hideout on Talos Island where the Magic Man ran off to. He also tells you that the Magic Man can jump through time thanks to his magic stop watch."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mission3Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P3885498924" "Amanda Gates ratted out her accomplice, the Magic Man, so you went over to Independence Port to question the Tsoo, figuring the Magic Man must be one of their leaders. As it turned out, the Tsoo were clueless, so you went after one of their leaders, a man by the name of Black Dragon. You infiltrated Black Dragon's illegal superadine shipping operation and forced him to tell you everything he knew about the Magic Man. According to him, the Magic Man was in the Family and worked for a man known as Jimmy the Preacher.<br><br>You went over to Jimmy the Preacher's office to ask him some questions. After busting through Jimmy's buttonmen you made him talk. He told you that the Magic Man used to just be a buttonman named Mickey Maloney until he started taking down the Tsoo like they were nothing. Jimmy promoted him and that's how he earned the nickname of the Magic Man.<br><br>You checked out the cargo ship that Jimmy the Preacher told you the Magic Man was headed to and walked into a gang war between the Family and the Tsoo. The ship was rigged with bombs, which you quickly disarmed, and then you took down the Family members to question them about where the Magic Man had gone.<br><br>Big Tony, the next highest guy in the Family pecking order, revealed that the Magic Man went over to a warehouse on Talos Island. He also told you about the Magic Man's ability to disappear. This was all the information Mercedes Sheldon needed in order to determine that the Magic Man had an artifact of hers called The Devil's Timepiece."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - TheMagicManSouvenirClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// tDetailString :
"P252348574" "As you look at the multiple pairs of Mickey Maloney's brass knuckles you remember a story you like to call, <color deepskyblue>the Magic Man</color><br><br><color red>Amanda Gates</color> ratted out her accomplice, <color red>the Magic Man</color>, so you went over to Independence Port to question the Tsoo, figuring the Magic Man must be one of their leaders. As it turned out, the Tsoo were clueless, so you went after one of their leaders, a man by the name of <color red>Black Dragon</color>. You infiltrated Black Dragon's illegal superadine shipping operation and forced him to tell you everything he knew about the Magic Man. According to him, the Magic Man was in the Family and worked for a man known as <color red>Jimmy the Preacher</color>.<br><br>You went over to Jimmy the Preacher's office to ask him some questions. After busting through Jimmy's buttonmen you made him talk. He told you that the Magic Man used to just be a buttonman named <color red>Mickey Maloney</color> until he started taking down the Tsoo like they were nothing. Jimmy promoted him and that's how he earned the nickname of the Magic Man.<br><br>You checked out the cargo ship that Jimmy the Preacher told you the Magic Man was headed to and walked into a gang war between the Family and the Tsoo. The ship was rigged with bombs, which you quickly disarmed, and then you took down the Family members to question them about where the Magic Man had gone.<br><br><color red>Big Tony</color>, the next highest guy in the Family pecking order, revealed that the Magic Man went over to a warehouse on Talos Island. He also told you about the Magic Man's ability to disappear. This was all the information Mercedes Sheldon needed in order to determine that the Magic Man had an artifact of hers called <color deepskyblue>The Devil's Timepiece</color>.<br><br>You snuck into the warehouse that the Magic Man had taken refuge inside only to find it crawling with Warriors. You fought through the Warriors and confronted the Magic Man, but soon realized the power of the Devil's Timepiece. No matter how many times you knocked the Magic Man down he kept coming back.<br><br>Ultimately the Magic Man defeated himself by going back in time to the same moment numerous times to create duplicates of himself. This caused a temporal paradox and rendered the magic of the Devil's Timepiece inert. You took down the Magic Man and recovered the artifact for Mercedes Sheldon. Your efforts saved many, but the most important thing you saved was the soul of Mickey Maloney."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P2875644859" "I'm sure you remember Amanda Gates, {HeroName}. It would seem she's ratted out one of her accomplices, someone in Independence Port called <color red>the Magic Man</color>. Some of my sources indicate that the Tsoo have been dropping that name lately.<br><br><color orange>Head over to Independence Port and question the Tsoo about the Magic Man.</color>"
// AcceptString :
"P660932626" "Question Tsoo"
// SendOffString :
"P2877493096" "According to Amanda she never met the Magic Man in person. She received <color deepskyblue>The Dirge of Chaos</color> in a package from him.<br><br>Whoever he is he definitely went through some effort to hide his identity and this is what has me worried. If the Magic Man has my family's artifacts and is doling them out to unscrupulous individuals we might have a serious problem on our hands."
// TaskTitle :
"P2206811752" "<color deepskyblue>The Magic Man</color>"
// TaskSubTitle :
"P2770291627" "<color deepskyblue>Part One</color>"

